<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Berbera</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Berbera is a port city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-aden">Gulf of Aden</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a>. A trading port since antiquity, it was long famous for an annual fair, held in the cool season, where caravans from the interior met merchants from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. It was the capital of British Somaliland until 1941, and its deep-water port remains Somaliland's main gateway.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/berbera.jpg" alt="Berbera" width="320" height="169" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Seepsimon · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Berbera_6666.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
